\f1\b\fs22 Blessed Mother meets Parliament
\f2\b0 \
2 to 3 weeks after bombing\
The rail car rolled slowly towards the nominated arrival/departure point where a crowd of Elvi, all clad in black, had gathered and were crying loudly and smacking themselves repeatedly in the forehead. Karate jumped down and grabbed the nearest black-clad Elvis, \'93What has happened, my sister?\'94\
\'93Oh, the Dawkins save us! One of the great Sages, Kleoboulos, is dead! Killed by the Jesus.\'94 She wept and recommenced smacking her forehead and pulling at her hair. \'93He gave his life to save our brothers.\'94 \
\'93How could this be? He was healthy just a few days ago.\'94 Karate descended into denial, but upon seeing his martial arts brothers crying and receiving comfort from the mourning throngs, he too succumbed to weeping. \'93The Dawkins save us.\'94\
Sarah grabbed Karate and looked him in the eye. \'93Elvis, your duty is to protect the keep of the great Sages.\'94 He did not respond. \'93Has anyone relieved you? No? Then get back to your duty, Elvis. Kleo would not want his home to be lost, um, to non-believers.\'94 She resisted the urge to roll her eyes.\
\'93Of course, you are correct, Blessed Mother. I will return to my duty immediately.\'94 Karate Elvis gathered together his security team and returned to the Travelator and stood to attention at the open door as the carriage faded into the distance. \
\'93That was impressive, Sarah. He was about to completely lose it.\'94 Chanta looked across the gathering of mourning Elvi and was amazed by the outpouring of grief for someone none of them knew.\
\'93I wanted to separate them from the rest of this mob. Can you imagine what would happen if he had told them what I was considering?\'94 She thought throwing octane onto this fire would lead to an unfortunate outcome.\
\'93This crowd would turned ugly, very quickly. Let\'92s find the other Sages.\'94 He grabbed her by the hand and waded into the crowd. \'93Much better than the last crush we were in, eh?\'94\
\'93Its just as claustrophobic.\'94 She was not keen on crowds anymore.\
\'93Oh, yeah?\'94 Chanta smirked. \'93Make way for the Blessed Mother. Blessed Mother coming through.\'94 The entire crowd stopped sobbing, split in half and dropped to their knees, leaving a wide pathway for the pair to freely stride their way through. \'93Not bad, huh?\'94\
 \
\'93Nicely done, but where do we go now?\'94 \
\'93The Blessed Mother wishes to see the great Sages. Where are they, my Elvi?\'94 All right index fingers pointed towards an imposing freestanding building. Formerly an Elvine brothel, the Vulva Las Vegas was now the seat of power in the Elvi Nation and recently renamed \'93Parliament House.\'94\
\'93The old brothel is parliament house?\'94 Chanta said, breaking into a smile. \'93The makes sense, there\'92ll still be a pack of cunts working there.\'94 He almost let out an uproarious laugh, but caught a glimpse of the mourning Elvis a decency managed to take hold. \'91Thanks guys. You can get back to your mourning now, but put your backs into it! I want to see some real emotion, c\'92mon.\'94 He turned to Sarah and shrugged. \'93It\'92s what the Great Teacher wants.\'94\
\'93Chanta, you might try a little restraint in the exercise of power.\'94\
\'93Call me the Great Teacher, Blessed Mother.\'94 Chanta liked the idea of being the subject of a little hero worship, even if his fans were completely delusional. \
\'93You are kidding, of course.\'94 The Blessed Mother was not amused.\
\'93Of course. Do you think I can take any of this seriously? I mean look at them.\'94 Chanta pointed his finger around, randomly pointing at individual Elvi, all balling their eyes out. \'93How dumb are these pricks? They didn\'92t even know Kleo.\'94\
\'93Yes, but you know what he and his colleagues did to me, they do not. I cannot mourn his death, but I understand their grief. They are children who have just lost a father and they are hurt. We must tread carefully here or see their grief flash over into anger without warning. I would strongly suggest you show a little respect even if you don\'92t have any for them.\'94\
\'93Of course you are right, but I think it is a little unfair to say I have no respect for the Elvi.\'94 Chanta always had difficultly taking anything seriously, in fact, the more serious a situation, the more jokes and ridiculous comments popped into his mind. He was unable to behave himself at a funeral or a wedding, blurting out anything that manifested in his head. \'93I love the Elvi. They are the only thing that makes this shit-filled city tolerable. I cannot imagine a world without Elvis.\'94 
\f3\i Imagine that, not one Elvis in the entire world!
\f2\i0 \
As they approached two Roman Elvis guards saluted and opened the massive wooden double doors of the main entrance of Parliament, revealing a cavernous atrium that echoed their footsteps and gasps of amazement. The formidable stone structure had housed the largest brothel and burlesque house in the PTD, sporting 50 rooms and 50 bathrooms, augmented with saunas, steam rooms, bars and restaurants, plus a 300 seat theatre. The advent of Elvi governance, saw all Elvine prostitutes freed from their servitude. Although some of the girls did not like sudden unemployment, the Elvi nation would not tolerate any of their number, male or female, being sexually exploited by the sick fucks the Primary Trade Dominion seemed to produce. The freehold title of the site was purchased by the Elvi taking a huge chunk from the treasury, but they were determined to end the exploitation no matter what the cost. \
The Parliamentary Sergeant-at-arms stood sentry upon the freshly polished marble floor outside the doors to the Chamber, an ornate silver coated gold mace held tightly in white gloves, across his chest. The bulbous bejewelled head of the metre long ceremonial weapon rested gently against the elaborate gold braided lapels of his gaudy red jacket, etchings of the Dawkins Holy Cypher and emblem of the Elvi dutifully pointed outward. As the VIP\'92s approached, he silently bowed low and ushered them into an ante-room to the side of the parliamentary chamber. \
\'93the High Elvis will be informed of your visit, Blessed Mother and Great Teacher, immediately. Please make yourselves comfortable. I apologise for the wait, great ones.\'94 He bowed and walked backwards three steps before he turned, striding confidently out the door. The High Elvis was in parliament with his cabinet and the two remaining Sages, debating revenue policy. The Sergeant-at-arms entered the chamber and stood respectfully silent as the Minister for Revenue completed his maiden speech.\
\'93\'85..and to fully fund the public works I propose to levy a modest tax on each Elvis. We are one hundred thousand strong and a 10% levy on income will collect 10 million per month. We will be financially self sufficient.\'94\
\'93What about taxation from the Primary Trade Dominion? They will want a piece of the action.\'94 The Finance Minister was not wrong.\
\'93We will invest the revenue collected along with our royalties on music sales in the Primary Trade Dominion, as a single player with some considerable clout. We will be able to take advantage of the tax concessions offered only to corporate players. The Elvi nation will make a profit on the investments and pay little or no tax to the PTD. If we invest wisely we can fund all our projects with the dividends alone.\'94\
\'93Make sure we spread our exposure.\'94 The Treasurer wanted the High Elvis to know he was keeping up.\
\'93Yes, I have already engaged the geniuses at \'91Spread Doctor\'92. They have been around since before the formation of the Dominion. Not many companies can say that.\'94\
\'93Is it compulsory?\'94 The Minister for the Arts inquired. The arts portfolio insisted that he stick his mitt our for money as often as possible without ever making a contribution to the economy. \'93The Tax?\'94\
\'93None of our motions have the force of law. It is purely voluntary, but I am confident my Elvi brothers and sisters will see the sense in raising revenue for public works that will make a difference to the amenity of our little enclave.\'94\
\'93Thank you, Minister.\'94 The Speaker pointed to the doorway. \'93The Chair recognises the Sgt at Arms.\'94\
\'93Mr Speaker, High Elvis. Please forgive my intrusion, but the Blessed Mother and the Great Teacher are in the parliamentary ante-room.\'94 The sergeant-at-arms was beside himself with excitement. 
\f3\i I met the Blessed Mother and the Great Teacher! 
\f2\i0 \
\'93The Dawkins be praised! This is truly a blessing on us all. The Blessed Mother, no less.\'94 the High Elvis was just as excited as the rest. All except for Solo and Chilo who sat quietly and exchanged looks of alarm. \'93Perhaps they will be kind enough to address parliament. Can you bring them to us?\'94 The Sergeant-at-arms disappeared. \'93Quick, Quick! We have to set out the chairs so as to reflect their holy status. Who outranks who?\'94\
\'93Well, they both outrank you!\'94 Homeland Security Elvis blurted out. The others looked around at each other, wondering who would break first, but it was the High Elvis that let go of a belly laugh first and they all joined in. Being an Elvis was heaps of fun. \
\'93Obviously, but between them?\'94 the High Elvis finally responded.\
\'93She\'92s carrying the one-after-the-one, but he\'92s the prophet of the one. I really don\'92t know.\'94 The Attorney General injected. Lawyers only ever muddy the waters, so it was not expected that the leading law officer of the Elvi would make a decision or, in fact, be of any assistance. \
\'93She\'92s pregnant, we have to give her the best chair.\'94 the High Elvis said, pointing to the only chair with a cushion, the Speaker\'92s chair. \'93Decision made. Now let\'92s get this room organised. She will sit in the good chair opposite you guys and I will sit to her left and slightly behind and the Great Teacher will be seated on her right.\'94 After a great deal of scraping and scratching of the floor, the chamber was set in a configuration that satisfied the structure and order demanded by the High Elvis.\
\
The Sergeant-at-arms had fetched the honoured guests and found himself standing in the presence of greatness, legendary figures on either flank and he was about to introduce them to parliament. His rise to such stratospheric heights was dizzying. He lifted his official hand that held the official club and officially bashed on the doors with the official three bangs, before entering and proudly announcing in a loud, clear Elvi voice, \'93Ladies and gentlemen, the Blessed Mother and the Great Teacher. Thank you, very much.\'94\
The cabinet, the High Elvis and the entirety of parliament in the fledgling Elvi Nation, all stood and clapped loudly, maintaining the ovation until both had been guided to their designated chairs and were comfortably seated. The smiles of the beaming faces and red raw hands testament to the reverence with which both visitors were held.\
\'93The last time I was in here it was a strip club.\'94 The Great Teacher whispered into Sarah\'92s ear. \'93Ah yes, Elvine the flexible.\'94\
\'93We thank you, High Elvis and your cabinet for your warm welcome.\'94 The Blessed Mother looked about the chamber, every face serenely smiling upon her. \'94The Great Teacher and I are honoured and humbled by the warm ovation from the chamber.\'94 \
\'93Thank you, thank you both for taking the time to visit us. Blessed Mother you carry the future of our civilisation, not just the Elvi Nation, but for the entire Primary Trade Dominion. You are most revered and most loved, by every Elvis.\'94 Sarah nodded in approval and the cabinet again clapped loudly. \'93Great Teacher, without your wise counsel we would never have coalesced into a nation. If it were not for your wise teachings, we would still be mere buskers, cabaret acts and bar tenders.\'94\
\'93We still are!\'94 Said a jovial Minister for External Affairs. All the cabinet laughed. \'93No, don\'92t laugh. I\'92ve got a gig tomorrow.\'94\
\'93We will never be able to repay the debt to you.\'94 the High Elvis managed not to chuckle, a feat of great discipline.\
\'93I don\'92t accept cheques, High Elvis, cash will be fine.\'94 The room burst into laughter and Chanta was pleased. He could do with a bit of cash, though.\
\'93Your sense of humour matches your greatness.\'94 the High Elvis laughed.\
\'93What about my good looks?\'94 This time no-one laughed, not even a titter. It seemed if you were not an Elvis, you were just plain ugly.\
\'93Thank you, Great Teacher.\'94 Sarah cut him off, his banter serving no purpose. \'93We have made the pilgrimage to the Quarter to discuss matters grave and we wish a private audience with the High Elvis and the two remaining Sages, Solo and Chilo. For the rest of parliament, please do not think we are ignoring you, I wish to meet with each of you in due course.\'94\
\'93You heard the Blessed Mother, please leave.\'94 The High Elvi ordered. They left in an orderly fashion and without question or complaint. Sarah was amazed. If she had tried to clear a boardroom in such a manner, she would have been thrown out the window. 
\f3\i These Elvi are obedient and polite. 
\f2\i0 \
\'93High Elvis we have a major issue that must be discussed. You have been told I am carrying the re-incarnation of the great Richard Dawkins\'94\
\'93Praise be to him.\'94 the High Elvis and the Sages automatically responded.\
\'93For the purposes of this conversation could you please try to keep the praising to a minimum? It is going to take forever otherwise.\'94 \
\'93Of course, Blessed Mother.\'94\
\'93Please call me Sarah.\'94\
\'93I cannot do that, Blessed Mother. You and the one-after-the-one are most important and most revered.\'94\
\'93So I keep hearing. Getting back to what I was saying. You have been told I am carrying the re-incarnation of The Dawkins. Don\'92t say it.\'94 She stared daggers around the chamber and no one dared to praise the Dawkins on this occasion. \'93I have confirmed that the DNA is largely that of Richard Dawkins, but do you know how he came to be gestating within me?\'94\
\'93We all assumed immaculate conception, Blessed Mother.\'94 the High Elvis quickly replied. \'93But it is certainly gratifying to hear that we can scientifically prove he is The Dawkins. The Elvi will rejoice.\'94\
\'93There may be no reason to rejoice. Solo? Chilo? Can you shed any light on this so-called immaculate conception?\'94 Sarah\'92s sarcasm dripped on the floor. \
\
\'93Our leader, the most revered Kleoboulos, was profoundly disturbed with the manner the Primary Trade Dominion had evolved.\'94 Solo began his confession. \'93He had a dream of a real democracy and an egalitarian society. He was once in the employ of a icon of our recent history, Jamison Hardy and they worked hard to improve the standard of living for all of us. After Jamison Hardy died, the Primary Trade Dominion, with no great leaders or visionaries, fell into disrepair. Greed became god and the gap between the wealthy and everyone else broadened to the point that we now have millions of working poor. The management class punishes anyone for lack of wealth. A boot stomping on a human face forever? That is nothing compared the punishment meted out to our poor, to us. Kleo decided we needed a new great leader and placed his faith in evolution, but evolution is slow, glacially slow and it was necessary to intervene. After many years he managed to procure an archived tissue sample of The Dawkins, praise be to him, and it was placed in a cloning unit for processing.\'94 \
\'93Where on earth would he get a tissue sample of a long dead Richard Dawkins?\'94 She wondered who would keep such an inventory?\
\'93Linus Grawling.\'94\
\'93Okay, yep. That makes sense.\'94 The Holy Mother saw everyone was nodding in agreement. Linus Grawling really got up to some sneaky shit and it was not too hard to believe he had been the author of this little disaster.\
Solo spoke very slowing, carefully and deliberately. He did not want to say anything that would upset Sarah any further, but he knew this was practically unavoidable. \'93When the Holy Mother and the Great Teacher presented themselves before us, some time ago, Kleo saw it as a sign from the universe. I could try to blame it all on Kleo, but we were all in agreement, the timing was perfect and we could not ignore what the universe had planted in front of us. I was the one who used the device upon you and I should be the one to suffer any punishment, even if that means death.\'94 Solo was sincere and Chilo placed his arm around his colleague in solidarity.\
\'93Thank you for your candor, I expected you to twist into a pretzel trying to justify yourself. Apart from the abject criminality and shocking immorality of your actions, we have another problem.\'94 Sarah stood up an began to walk around the room and behind Solo and Chilo. \'93On the same night you pair assaulted me, I was exposed to a biological agent, artificial DNA, it did not harm me, but it has attached itself to the foetal Dawkins on a genetic level. I have had the genome of this child mapped and there is clearly extra pieces of genetic information added to the helix. In short, no-one can say, with any degree of accuracy, how this child will develop. Technically, it isn\'92t even human and may not resemble anything like a human being. I have been made very aware the importance this child has for the Elvi nation, but what do I do? Produce for them a mutant? Do I terminate the pregnancy and walk away? Do I roll the dice and have the child? Do I even want a child? I wasn\'92t asked. I had a child literally forced into me. Do I want to be a single mother? What are my career prospects as a single mother? What happens if it is a monster? The questions are unending.\'94\
 \
\'93I cannot tell you what to do. Kleo would have, no doubt, been most insistent on the child being brought to full term and given the opportunity of life.\'94 Solo did not want to be the cause of any further damage.\
\'93That is just avoidance, Solo. I have been mulling this over and I am torn in every direction at once. I want to hear what you have to say before I decide what to do with the child and what to do with you.\'94 \
\'93The possibility that the child will be born deformed is concerning, very concerning. I think this all is also an opportunity, presented by pure luck, of course, but an opportunity nevertheless. On that night three fateful and unusual events occurred. You stumbled into our car on the travelator. The odds are 7200 to 1 that you would find us. You could have just as easily have been killed in another car. Secondly you arrived on a very auspicious night for us and you fitted the profile perfectly. We had been circling the city, searching for someone like you for years. Thirdly the bio-agent seems to be interested in the Dawkins clone, but not you. This seems very peculiar. All that in one night? The odds must be astronomical! Perhaps it was meant to happen. I don\'92t believe in signs, but I think the universe has served up a particularly unusual set of circumstances and a difficult choice.\'94 Solo sighed lightly and ran his fingers slowly through his unwashed hair, damp with sweat. \'93The child is a potent symbol that has brought the Elvi together as one - and he is yet to be born. Can you imagine what he will achieve after he is born? I fear depriving the Elvi of their leader will cause great upheaval across the entire Elvi Nation. The High Elvis can tell us how the Elvi might respond.\'94\
\'93Blessed Mother, every clone, every Elvis is sterile and can never know the delight of having children of their own. The thought of aborting any child requires at least some moral justification, but the thought of The Dawkins being ripped from us is intolerable. The reaction would be as violent as it would be indiscriminate. I am not so ignorant as to be unaware of the pro-choice stance of the rest of the PTD, but I am not among that number and neither are my Elvi brothers or sisters. I think I can say, on behalf of every Elvis, that we look forward to the arrival of The Dawkins and we don\'92t care if he has three heads and tentacles.\'94 the High Elvis was again amazed at the conundrums that presented themselves to him. 
\f3\i Did these issues exist before we formed a parliament?
\f2\i0  \
\'93I will not be told what to do with my body by a group of men.\'94 Sarah said, raising her voice in pitch and volume. 
\f3\i Although I did ask.
\f2\i0 \
\'93With the greatest respect Blessed Mother, this is why I was reluctant to to offer any advice. We all may have differing views on abortion, generally, but I would suggest, again most reluctantly, that issues relating to terminations should be determined on a case by case basis. I have no doubt a termination has a profound effect on all concerned, but this would deeply scar in excess of 100,000 people, not to mention the blood that will be shed. But no matter what we or anyone else says, you have to make the final determination.\'94 Solo was trying walk tightrope. He knew he should have kept his mouth shut.\
\'93Oh, you acknowledge my dominion over my own body now, but where was that when we met? I would not be in this position if it was not for you and your silly ideology. Yes, I said silly! You must think you possess a special brand of righteous need to justify a forced pregnancy. It was no better that raping a girl in her sleep.\'94 Sarah was now livid and ready to let rip. No matter what angle she looked at it, she was the victim of rape and that was justification enough to terminate. However, the reaction from the Elvi could not be ignored. 100,000 insane musicians on a rampage did not make for pleasant dreams, then again neither did giving birth to 
\f3\i The Fly
\f2\i0 . \'93Precisely what were you trying to achieve endlessly circling the city? What you failed to do over a period of years, Chanta here managed in a few hours\'85.while drunk!\'94\
\'93I do not offer up a defence for my actions that night. Kleo was a most powerful personality, but I will not evade culpability. The events since have unfolded the way Kleo predicted, with the exception, of course, of the bio-agent. We could not have predicted that intervening event.\'94 Solo remained calm. He had resigned himself to a terrible fate.\
\'93I do not have to make my decision right at this moment, but whatever decision I make, you are all forbidden to speak of this ever again. As for Solo and Chilo, what should be done? I could go just complain to the PTD police. In fact, I have been contracting for them and could arrange a very unpleasant and lengthy incarceration, but being a rape victim I would be exposed to ridicule and my career prospects would be ruined. I would be expected to terminate the pregnancy in any case. No level 5 could bring a child of rape into the world - he would be treated as a leper. So, I ask, what do we do with you two?\'94 Sarah had nothing and hoped someone in the room could offer some assistance.\
\'93You have got to at least shoot them. I did nothing and you shot me! I got hit three times, check it out.\'94 Chanta lifted his shirt to show off his war-wounds, but the skin had almost entirely repaired with only the slightest sign of 3 pale pink circles where the blasts had entered. \
\'93What do you think High Elvis?\'94 Punishing the Sages was not something Sarah was prepared to do unilaterally. \
\'93Thank you, Blessed Mother. Crime and punishment is an issue that the cabinet and I have found quite vexing. Five of our number were infected by the Jesus recently and how to deal with them was much discussed. We did not form any solid crime policy, but the cabinet was of the unanimous opinion that we do not possess the legal authority or the special morality required to punish anyone.\'94 the High Elvis recalled with noticeable anguish. \'93We find capital punishment and torture completely abhorrent. It was decided that we could not incarcerate our brothers for the purposes of punishment, however, we found it acceptable to offer them treatment and detain them for their own safety. We sent for the great Sages and they cured all five, but Kleoboulos died during the final stages of the treatment. He gave his life for the Elvi and the Sages will always be honoured among our number. I cannot bring myself to incarcerate Kleoboulos\'92 apprentices, they could just as easily been killed along with him. They were prepared to give their lives as well.\'94\
\'93We can\'92t execute them, torture them or incarcerate them?\'94 Sarah sighed with exasperation.\
\'93Are we allowed to tickle them?\'94 Chanta laughed alone. 
\f3\i I started well, but since then, every joke a swing and a miss.
\f2\i0 \
\'93If I may, Blessed Mother.\'94 the High Elvis was having a light bulb moment. \'93I have commenced a regime of public works in the Quarter, its mostly busy work, but important to improve the amenity and aroma of our home. The travelator is a resource that could be useful if it managed properly. With your permission I would like to set Solo and Chilo a task difficult and, I think, important.\'94 \
\'93I am listening High Elvis.\'94 Sarah was glad to hear any suggestion.\
\'93The travelator is overrun with criminals of all kinds and I proposed that Solo and Chilo lead my Elvi in taking it back. They will no doubt encounter violent resistance and I expect some of my Elvi brothers will die. I want the Elvi to take control of the Travelator, I want at least one Elvi in each car and I want to make public transport safe. Blessed Mother, what say you?\'94 High Elvis hope the Blessed Mother would be in agreement.\
\'93I cannot think of anything better at this point.\'94 Sarah appeared relieved. \'93Solo, Chilo was do you think?\'94\
\'93The Dawkins be praised! We would be honoured to take on such an important task.\'94 Solo said. \'93Safe transport within the Primary Trade Dominion? That is something to strive for and something to be proud of.\'94\
\'93I will put all my efforts into this assignment, High Elvis. There are about 7200 cars and we will need considerable resources, but I am happy to assist.\'94 Chilo chimed in. \'93The truth be the Dawkins and the Dawkins be the truth.\'94\
\'93I know that this cannot excuse us for what we have done to you Blessed Mother, but I hope this may, in some small way, place us on the road to atonement.\'94 Solo was again sincere, wearing a long, pale mask of regret.\
\'93It will be a long time, Solo.\'94 Sarah was not yet anywhere near forgiving them and thought she never would. \'93Well Great Teacher, I think we have achieved all we are going to achieve here today. Shall we take out leave?\'94 \
\'93Yes, it has been another very long day.\'94 Chanta wanted to get back to Sarah\'92s new apartment. He had only ever contracted for corporate gigs and had never seen the inside of a manager\'92s private residence before, much less live in it.\
\'93Blessed Mother, the funeral for Kleoboulos will be held today. I would like you to participate in the ceremony and afterwards we will be having the biggest wake that has ever been held in the quarter.\'94 the High Elvis was very keen to be seen in public rubbing shoulders with the Blessed Mother, The Great Teacher and the Sages. \'93It would be my greatest honour to have you all as my guests at my table for the wake.\'94\
\'93Thank you for your kind invitation, but\'85..\'94 Sarah said before being suddenly cut off.\
\'93Yes, thank you. We would be delighted.\'94 The lure of free piss was too much for Chanta to ignore and he did not want to be a part of insulting the High Elvis. Sarah\'92s apartment could wait.\
\'93We are supposed to meet up with Hayley later this evening.\'94 Sarah whispered.\
\'93High Elvis, may we invite the Holy Aunts to the wake?\'94 Chanta smirked. \'93They are both sworn protectors of the one-after-the-one and rest high in our esteem.\'94 He desperately wanted to rolls his eyes.\
\'93The Holy Aunties? Of Course, I would be honoured to meet them both.\'94 the High Elvis replied. More V.I.P\'92s meant greater exposure for him and he was very pleased.\
\'93I have said it before and I\'92ll say it again, Sarah.\'94 Chanta whispered into her ear. \'93How dumb are these pricks?\'94\
\'93Keep it down, Chanta. I will contact Hayley and I guess the other sworn protector is our self-medicating pathologist? You can try to get hold of her, if she is in any condition to answer a call. Holy Aunties, really?\'94\
\'93It\'92s what came to mind.\'94
